  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes and preferring the lottery with the higher probability. The individual considers the near-certainty of a positive outcome in A (100%) versus the 99% chance in B (since B has a 1% chance of 0). This aligns directly with the core of the decision reason—evaluating the likelihood of a favorable (non-zero) outcome and favoring the safer option. Although the individual expresses this in terms of risk aversion and personal valuation ('nicht wert'), the underlying comparison is probabilistic and matches the structure of the reason. The justification, while subjective in tone, is based on a comparison of outcome probabilities, particularly the risk of getting nothing. Therefore, the information considered and the justification are consistent with the decision reason. There is strong evidence that the individual used a probability-based comparison focused on the chance of a favorable outcome.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
